{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Cut Citizenship Fees for 20+ Year Residents& Exempt UK-Educated Adults From LITU",
        "additional_details": "Many people moved to the UK as young children and have spent their lives studying, working and paying taxes here. The UK is the only home many have ever known. After 20+ years of residence, high citizenship fees create an unnecessary financial barrier. Those educated in UK schools should not need a Life in the UK test to prove their knowledge of British life. Long-term residence and education should be recognised, making citizenship more affordable and accessible.",
        "background": "We ask the Government to waive British citizenship application fees for people who have lived continuously in the UK for 20 years or more. We also ask for an exemption from the Life in the UK test for adults who completed their full education in the UK.",
